From 84044cd7d4d96c3151a8656a4f1b59c115a81f34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: postmarketOS klte experiment <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:41:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] media: rc: add the Samsung Galaxy S5 iCE40 IR
 transmitter

The IR blaster of the Galaxy S5 (klte) is an IR LED driven by a Lattice
iCE40 FPGA. The FPGA is configured at probe time by shifting its
bitstream in over two GPIOs; the same lines are then used as a
bit-banged I2C bus to hand the FPGA a carrier frequency and a list of
pulse/space lengths in carrier cycles. A status GPIO reports that the
packet checksum was accepted (low) and that the emission finished (high).

Protocol and sequencing follow Samsung's downstream
drivers/misc/ice40xx.c. The device is exposed as a raw LIRC
transmitter, so ir-ctl and friends work unchanged.
---
 drivers/media/rc/Kconfig            |  13 +
 drivers/media/rc/Makefile           |   1 +
 drivers/media/rc/ir-ice40-samsung.c | 399 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 413 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/media/rc/ir-ice40-samsung.c

